{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22505 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Camellidin I appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step pathway that ultimately targets Thrombopoietin. The evidence suggests that Camellidin I interacts with Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which is then targeted by two different compounds—Spicatin and Npc118323—both of which in turn direct their activity toward Thrombopoietin. This indicates that Camellidin I may modulate the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways that lead to Thrombopoietin production. The shared target of these compounds and the consistent interaction with Lysine-specific demethylase 2A suggest a possible mechanism involving enzyme regulation or signaling modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A as a critical mediator in the relationship between Camellidin I and Thrombopoietin, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
